{title: Secret Garden}
{artist: Bruce Springsteen}
{key: C}

{c: Verse 1}
[C]Shell let you in her house,        if you come [F]knockin late at night,
[Am]Shell let you in her mouth,        if the [F]words you say are right,
[C]If you pay the price,        shell [F]let you deep inside,
Theres a [Am]secret [G]garden,        she [C]hides.
[C]Shell let you in her car,        to go [F]drivin around,
[Am]Shell let you into parts of herself,        [F]thatll bring you down,
[C]Shell let you in her heart,        if you [F]got a hammer and a vice,
But her [Am]secret [G]garden,        dont [C]think twice.
[Am]Youve gone a [F]million miles,        [C]how fard you [G]get,
[Am]To that place where [F]you cant remember,        [C]and you cant [G]forget,
[C]Shell lead you down a path,        therell [F]be tenderness in the air,
[Am]Shell let you come just far enough,        so you [F]know shes really there.
[C]Shell look at you and smile,        and [F]her eyes will say.
[Am]Shes got a secret garden,        [F]where everything you want.
[C]Where everything you need,        [F]will always stay,
a [Am]million [G]miles a [C]way.
